  "result": "The concept `drv.interaction.passing_on_right` now passes the gate with **OK** (3 witnesses, 4 atoms read), using 4 of the 6 gate runs.\n\n**The body:** at each observation, all four of these must hold:\n- the two road users head the same way, within `cos_tol`;\n- their overlap along a's heading is at least zero, so they are side by side;\n- b is strictly to a's left;\n- a's speed is greater than b's speed plus `speed_tol` (strictly greater).\n\nThe contract decided every one of these readings, so there are no narrowings.\n\n**The witnesses:** two eastbound cars, with b 4 m to a's left, over three instants 1 s apart. The instance uses `cos_tol` = 0.98 and `speed_tol` = 0.5 m/s.\n- **holds:** a at 12 m/s, b at 10 m/s, side by side the whole time.\n- **fails:** a at 8 m/s, b at 10 m/s.\n- **blind:** the holds trace with `rel.longitudinal_overlap` masked, and the source also reports no body extents or occupancy. This was needed because masking that relation only removes a value the source supplied. Core still calculates the overlap from the two cars' outlines, so the scenario first came out compliant. Then the trace was rejected because a car with observed occupancy must have an outline, so occupancy is unobserved too. The body reads neither extents nor occupancy, so the overlap is still the only unknown.\n\n**Gate runs:**\n1. WITNESS_FAIL: blind came out compliant.\n2. The same failure again. I ran the gate by mistake when I meant to read a Core file, which used up one run.\n3. WITNESS_FAIL: the trace was rejected because of the occupancy issue.\n4. OK.\n\nTwo other shell commands were blocked because only the gate command is allowed: a `grep` over Core and a `harness --help`. I read the Core files with the Read tool instead.\n\nFiles are in `library/` and in the working directory:\n- `TrafficSpec/Concepts/interaction/passing_on_right.lean`\n- `TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/interaction/passing_on_right.lean`\n- `task_result.md`",
